  "Number": 5,
  "Question": "Which of the following is equal to the product\n\n\\[ \\begin{aligned} &\\dfrac{8}{4} \\cdot \\dfrac{12}{8} \\cdot \\dfrac{16}{12} \\cdots \\dfrac{4n+4}{4n} \\\\ &\\quad \\cdots \\dfrac{2008}{2004}? \\end{aligned} \\]",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(251\\)",
    "B": "\\(502\\)",
    "C": "\\(1004\\)",
    "D": "\\(2008\\)",
    "E": "\\(4016\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "Each numerator except the last is the denominator of the next fraction. Thus every number from \\(8\\) through \\(2004\\) appearing in the product cancels once above and once below. All these numbers are positive, so the cancellations are valid. Only the first denominator, \\(4\\), and the last numerator, \\(2008\\), remain:\n\\[\n\\frac84\\cdot\\frac{12}{8}\\cdot\\frac{16}{12}\\cdots\\frac{2008}{2004}\n=\\frac{2008}{4}=502.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(502\\), choice \\(B\\).",
